Luxstream pairing: no PIN for the user to carry between the two machines.

Stock Moonlight shows a four-digit PIN and asks the user to type it into the
host's Web UI before pairing completes.  In Luxstream the host is configured to
answer the pairing handshake with a fixed PIN on its own (PAIRING_PIN in
Sunshine's src/nvhttp.cpp, changed separately), so there is no code to read off
one screen and type into the other.  This patch removes the dialog that would
otherwise sit there waiting for an answer that is never needed.

Two files change:
  app/backend/computermanager.cpp   generatePinString() returns "0000"
  app/gui/PcView.qml                pairing dialog is no longer opened

Both sides must agree on the PIN.  Changing only this patch leaves pairing
failing with "The PIN from the PC didn't match".

Apply from the root of a moonlight-qt checkout:
  git apply moonlight-bez-pina.patch
  # or: patch -p1 < moonlight-bez-pina.patch

The patch is written against LF sources; with core.autocrlf=true a plain
"git apply" rewrites the whole file to CRLF.  Disable the conversion if that
matters:
  git -c core.autocrlf=false apply moonlight-bez-pina.patch

QML is compiled into qml_qmlcache.qrc inside Moonlight.exe, so the client has to
be recompiled for the dialog to actually disappear.

diff --git a/app/backend/computermanager.cpp b/app/backend/computermanager.cpp
index 96177da..ca9f489 100644
--- a/app/backend/computermanager.cpp
+++ b/app/backend/computermanager.cpp
@@ -1005,7 +1005,12 @@ void ComputerManager::addNewHost(NvAddress address, bool mdns, QString name, NvA
 
 QString ComputerManager::generatePinString()
 {
-    return QString::asprintf("%04u", QRandomGenerator::system()->bounded(10000));
+    // Luxstream: the host answers the pairing handshake with this same fixed PIN
+    // on its own (see PAIRING_PIN in Sunshine's src/nvhttp.cpp), so there is no
+    // four-digit code for a human to carry from one machine to the other.
+    // Changing one side without the other breaks pairing with
+    // "The PIN from the PC didn't match".
+    return QStringLiteral("0000");
 }
 
 #include "computermanager.moc"
diff --git a/app/gui/PcView.qml b/app/gui/PcView.qml
index e80135c..02058ee 100644
--- a/app/gui/PcView.qml
+++ b/app/gui/PcView.qml
@@ -235,12 +235,11 @@ CenteredGridView {
                 else {
                     var pin = computerModel.generatePinString()
 
-                    // Kick off pairing in the background
+                    // Luxstream: the host accepts this fixed PIN by itself, so
+                    // pairing runs entirely in the background. There is no code
+                    // for the user to copy into the host's Web UI, hence no PIN
+                    // dialog. Failures still surface via pairingComplete().
                     computerModel.pairComputer(index, pin)
-
-                    // Display the pairing dialog
-                    pairDialog.pin = pin
-                    pairDialog.open()
                 }
             } else if (!model.online) {
                 // Using open() here because it may be activated by keyboard
